WEBVTT

00:00:19.108 --> 00:00:20.693
(SNORING)

00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:23.112
(RINGTONE PLAYING)

00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:24.238
I'm awake, I'm awake!

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.533
Hey, Buster.

00:00:27.616 --> 00:00:28.993
BUSTER: Hey, Eddie.

00:00:29.076 --> 00:00:30.703
Man, where'd you go? Are you okay?

00:00:30.786 --> 00:00:34.081
Listen, could you meet me
at the corner of Dinsdale and Lemington?

00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:35.457
(YAWNS) Now?

00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:36.917
Yeah, please.

00:00:37.418 --> 00:00:38.919
And could you...

00:00:39.003 --> 00:00:41.380
Ahem. Could you bring me a spare Speedo?

00:00:41.463 --> 00:00:42.464
(CALL DISCONNECTS)

00:00:42.548 --> 00:00:43.757
Speedo?

00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:51.515
Hey, Miss Crawly.

00:00:51.682 --> 00:00:53.434
Oh! Hello, Eddie!

00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:55.144
Hey, did you bring the Speedo?

00:00:55.352 --> 00:00:57.688
The... Oh, yeah. Uh, here.

00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:00.149
-Great. You're a real pal, Eddie.
-(HORN HONKING)

00:01:01.692 --> 00:01:03.736
Oh! Our first customer!

00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:05.196
-(CHUCKLES)
-Miss Crawly, fill the bucket.

00:01:05.279 --> 00:01:06.322
Be right with you, sir.

00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:09.283
Wait, what are you doing?

00:01:09.491 --> 00:01:11.243
-The only other job I know.
-(HORN BLARING)

00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:16.874
(SIGHS) I'm just glad
my dad isn't here to see this.

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:19.835
-Miss Crawly, if you would...
-Oh!

00:01:21.086 --> 00:01:22.087
Thanks.

00:01:22.171 --> 00:01:24.340
Well, gotta go to work.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.091
Uh, I'll see you around, Eddie.

00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:27.259
(OPERA MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:41.857 --> 00:01:43.192
(ENGINE STARTS)

00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:46.528
Come on! I ain't got all day!

00:01:46.862 --> 00:01:47.988
(PANICKED GRUNTING)

00:01:48.113 --> 00:01:49.198
Aw, forget it.

00:01:49.365 --> 00:01:50.824
-(ENGINE STARTS)
-Too slow, dude.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.034
Whoa!

00:01:53.244 --> 00:01:54.662
(BRAKES SQUEAKING)

00:01:55.663 --> 00:01:56.664
(HORN HONKS)

00:01:57.539 --> 00:01:58.874
EDDIE: One moment, please, sir!

00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:02.503
Well, you know the good thing
about hitting rock bottom?

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:06.423
There's only one way left to go. And that's up.

00:02:07.216 --> 00:02:09.593
Come on. You wash. I'll dry.

00:02:13.806 --> 00:02:15.641
Thank you, Miss Crawly.

00:02:22.856 --> 00:02:24.066
(SQUEAKING)

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.578
(GLASS SQUEAKING)

00:02:39.665 --> 00:02:42.251
(MELODIOUS SINGING IN DISTANCE)

00:02:56.015 --> 00:02:57.391
Buster, where you going?

00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:00.060
(MEENA SINGING FOLK ROCK SONG)

00:03:39.475 --> 00:03:40.476
(GASPS)

00:03:41.685 --> 00:03:43.270
I, uh... (CLEARS THROAT)

00:03:44.229 --> 00:03:46.982
Do you think you could
sing like that in front of a real audience?

00:03:47.816 --> 00:03:51.195
I don't know. But I wanna try.

00:03:51.612 --> 00:03:53.030
Good. (CHUCKLES)

00:03:53.113 --> 00:03:54.239
'Cause I wanna see it.

00:03:56.116 --> 00:03:58.494
-We are? Seriously?
-(PIGLETS SHOUTING)

00:03:58.619 --> 00:04:01.121
Oh, my gosh! Okay, yes. I'll be right over.

00:04:02.206 --> 00:04:03.832
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

00:04:03.916 --> 00:04:05.292
Hello?

00:04:05.417 --> 00:04:06.752
Oh, hello, Mr. Moon.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.590
NEWS REPORTER DOG: (ON TV) Some say
he's the worst showman this city's ever seen.

00:04:11.673 --> 00:04:13.217
Some say he's a walking disaster.

00:04:13.384 --> 00:04:15.469
A loose cannon.

00:04:15.552 --> 00:04:16.720
Well, tomorrow night,

00:04:16.845 --> 00:04:20.933
the name Buster Moon will go down
in entertainment history once and for all,

00:04:21.016 --> 00:04:24.728
as he and this bunch of bumbling amateurs
attempt to re-stage the show

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.272
that brought down his theater.

00:04:28.982 --> 00:04:29.983
(INAUDIBLE)

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.111
Ah, don't you worry, Mike, all is forgiven.

00:05:14.194 --> 00:05:15.487
Just glad you're back in one piece.

00:05:15.571 --> 00:05:16.822
Oh, yeah, you're too kind, Mr. Moon.

00:05:16.905 --> 00:05:18.949
And, uh, the prize money?

00:05:19.032 --> 00:05:21.118
I mean, it's real this time, right?

00:05:21.201 --> 00:05:23.454
There is no prize money
'cause there's no competition.

00:05:23.537 --> 00:05:24.955
Tonight, you're singing for yourselves.

00:05:25.038 --> 00:05:26.748
Two minutes, everybody! Final checks.

00:05:26.832 --> 00:05:28.000
Singing for ourselves?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.335
(LAUGHS) Unbelievable.

00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:32.671
Who's he... This is crazy. I'm outta here.

00:05:33.255 --> 00:05:34.715
Hello!

00:05:34.798 --> 00:05:37.426
We're putting on a show here.

00:05:37.509 --> 00:05:39.636
You all should come and see it!

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.263
You! Come on!

00:05:41.388 --> 00:05:43.849
Come on, fella! It's gonna be really good!

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:47.269
Hey! How's our new stagehand getting on?

00:05:47.352 --> 00:05:48.395
He's learning fast.

00:05:48.479 --> 00:05:50.772
All set and standing by! I love this headset!

00:05:50.856 --> 00:05:52.858
The audience are in their seats, Mr. Moon.

00:05:52.941 --> 00:05:53.942
Great!

00:05:54.568 --> 00:05:55.861
-Hmm.
-(PIGLETS CHATTERING LOUDLY)

00:05:56.111 --> 00:05:57.154
NORMAN: Caspar!

00:05:57.237 --> 00:05:58.697
-BUSTER: That's all?
-Get your pants back on, young man!

00:05:59.698 --> 00:06:02.743
Please, you guys, please. Please sit down!

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.828
Hey! Put your shoes back on right now!

00:06:04.912 --> 00:06:07.289
Zoe, I saw that! Stop it!

00:06:07.539 --> 00:06:10.375
And, Leo, that is disgusting.

00:06:10.626 --> 00:06:13.420
Well, John, I've covered
many disasters for this network,

00:06:13.504 --> 00:06:14.755
but this is sure to...

00:06:14.838 --> 00:06:16.632
-(TRUMPETS PLAYING)
-Oh, they're about to start.

00:06:16.715 --> 00:06:18.425
Okay, guys, listen up!

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:20.302
Look, I gotta tell you, um,

00:06:20.385 --> 00:06:23.430
there's not much of
an audience out there tonight.

00:06:23.514 --> 00:06:25.015
But you know what?

00:06:25.098 --> 00:06:26.475
It doesn't matter.

00:06:26.642 --> 00:06:28.519
It really doesn't.

00:06:28.685 --> 00:06:31.313
'Cause tonight is our night.

00:06:31.522 --> 00:06:33.190
And whatever happens,

00:06:34.149 --> 00:06:37.486
I just want you all to know
how proud I am to be a part of this with you.

00:06:38.111 --> 00:06:39.488
Good luck, Mr. Moon.

00:06:39.738 --> 00:06:40.822
Good luck, everyone... Whoa!

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:45.369
(PANTING)

00:06:45.619 --> 00:06:46.912
Whoop! Uh...

00:06:46.995 --> 00:06:48.747
Sorry. Just jumped the cue there.

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.999
Don't worry. I'm gonna get the hang of this.

00:06:54.962 --> 00:06:56.713
(SIGHS DEEPLY)

00:06:56.797 --> 00:06:58.006
Here we go.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.473
All creatures great and small...

00:07:06.557 --> 00:07:08.350
-(PIGLETS LAUGHING)
-...welcome to the...

00:07:10.227 --> 00:07:11.520
Oh, hello, there.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.564
-(LAUGHS)
-Great!

00:07:13.689 --> 00:07:16.483
Welcome to our newly refurbished,
open-air theater.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.193
You ready, big guy?

00:07:18.318 --> 00:07:19.403
Yeah.

00:07:19.486 --> 00:07:20.946
I'm, like, totally ready.

00:07:21.029 --> 00:07:22.197
All right!

00:07:23.115 --> 00:07:24.366
Let's do this.

00:07:24.658 --> 00:07:26.618
Gunter and Rosita!

00:07:26.702 --> 00:07:27.786
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:07:31.707 --> 00:07:33.750
(SINGING POP SONG)

00:07:43.552 --> 00:07:45.095
(SINGING)

00:07:45.262 --> 00:07:46.597
(LAUGHING)

00:07:53.729 --> 00:07:55.439
(CHUCKLES) Are you getting this?

00:07:55.522 --> 00:07:57.858
(SINGING)

